module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaImageQuotient
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.LocalObjects

/-!
# The kernel `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` of the Yoneda localization, and the acyclics

Let `C` be a differential graded category over a commutative ring `R`, let
`Φ = K(h) : K(C) ⥤ K(Mod^dg(C))` be the differential graded Yoneda functor on homotopy
categories, let `G : ι → C.Obj` be a family of objects of `C` and let

`N = ⟨h_{G i}⟩`, `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`

be the localizing subcategory of `K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by the representables attached to `G`
and its preimage in `K(C)`, as in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/RightModule/YonedaImageQuotient.lean`. The
localization `DGCategory.RightModule.isLocalization_yonedaLift_comp` is taken at `Z` on the
nose, and identifying its target with the derived category of an abelian category asks for `Z`
to be the class of acyclic objects. This file settles both inclusions, for an arbitrary
`Ac : ObjectProperty C.K` playing the part of the acyclics.

## `Ac ≤ Z`

This holds as soon as `G` enumerates `Ac` up to isomorphism in `K(C)`, and it is formal:
`h_{G i}` is a *generator* of `N`, so it lies in `N` with nothing to prove, and `Z` is closed
under isomorphisms because `N` is. This is `DGCategory.RightModule.le_yonedaInverseImage`, with
the tautological enumeration by the subtype of `Ac` as
`DGCategory.RightModule.le_yonedaInverseImage_subtypeVal`.

What is *not* true, and is a different statement, is that `h_X` is an acyclic differential
graded module when `X` is an acyclic complex: by full faithfulness of `Φ` and
`DGCategory.RightModule.forall_hom_eq_zero_iff_isAcyclic`, the module `h_X` is acyclic exactly
when `Hom_{K(C)}(Y, X⟦n⟧) = 0` for every `Y` and every `n`, that is exactly when `X` is a zero
object of `K(C)`. Membership in `N` is membership in a localizing subcategory *generated by*
representables, not acyclicity of a module, and it is the former that defines `Z`.

## `Z ≤ Ac`

The route taken here replaces the Neeman–Thomason description of the compact objects of a
compactly generated localizing subcategory — the argument sketched in `YonedaImageQuotient.lean`,
which is not available in this development — by orthogonality against the objects that `Ac` is
orthogonal to, in the intended reading the `K`-injective complexes. It has two halves, and
neither mentions compactness.

* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_le_leftOrthogonal`: if every `G i` is left
  orthogonal to a shift-stable `D : ObjectProperty C.K`, then so is every object of `Z`. The
  input is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.rightOrthogonal_localizingClosure_iff'`, the criterion
  that an object is local for `N` as soon as the generators see nothing in it in any degree:
  applied to `h_Y` for `Y` in `D` it puts `h_Y` in `N^⊥`, and then `h_X ∈ N` forces every map
  `h_X ⟶ h_Y` to vanish. Full faithfulness of `Φ` (`DGCategory.full_yonedaOnK`,
  `DGCategory.faithful_yonedaOnK`) passes between `Hom_{K(C)}(X, Y)` and `Hom(h_X, h_Y)` in both
  directions.

  Taking `D = Ac.rightOrthogonal` and `G` a family of objects of `Ac`, this gives `Z ≤ ᗮ(Acᗮ)`
  with no hypothesis on `Ac` beyond stability under the shift.

* `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_resolution`:
  `ᗮ(Acᗮ) ≤ Ac` as soon as every object of `K(C)` admits an `Ac`-resolution, that is a morphism
  `f : X ⟶ Z` with `Z` right orthogonal to `Ac` and cone in `Ac`. In the intended reading this
  is the existence of `K`-injective resolutions, [Stacks, Tag 079P] for a Grothendieck abelian
  category. The proof is three lines: `f` vanishes because `X` is left orthogonal to `Z`, so the
  rotated triangle splits and `X⟦1⟧` is a retract of the cone.

Together, `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq` is the equality `Z = Ac` under those
two hypotheses: `G` enumerates `Ac`, and `Ac`-resolutions exist.

## Relation to the semiorthogonal decompositions of Tag 0H0P

`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_localizationTriangle`
below is the implication `(3) → (2)` of
`ObjectProperty.tfae_isRightAdmissible_isLeftAdmissible_extensionProduct_and_isEquivalence_ι_comp`
in `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Triangulated/AdmissibleSubcategories.lean`, for the pair
`(Ac, Ac.rightOrthogonal)`, whose hypothesis `Ac.extensionProduct Ac.rightOrthogonal = ⊤` is the
hypothesis stated here. It is proved directly rather than quoted because the direct proof needs
of `Ac` only stability under retracts, where the equivalence there also asks for closure under
isomorphisms and the shift, and because only the inclusion is wanted. The two are the places to
point at each other when these files are next deduplicated.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_localizationTriangle`
  and `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_resolution`:
  `ᗮ(Pᗮ) ≤ P` from localization triangles, respectively from resolutions.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.le_yonedaInverseImage`: the inclusion `Ac ≤ Z`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_le_leftOrthogonal` and
  `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_le`: the inclusion `Z ≤ Ac`.
* `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq`: the equality `Z = Ac`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 079P](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/079P)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

open Category Limits Pretriangulated

universe v u

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroObject C] [HasShift C ℤ] [Preadditive C]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C]

/-- **`ᗮ(Pᗮ) ≤ P` from localization triangles.** If every object `X` sits in a distinguished
triangle `W ⟶ X ⟶ Z ⟶ W⟦1⟧` with `W` in `P` and `Z` right orthogonal to `P`, then an object
left orthogonal to everything right orthogonal to `P` lies in `P`.

The morphism `X ⟶ Z` vanishes, so the identity of `X` factors through `W ⟶ X`, exhibiting `X`
as a retract of `W`. -/
lemma leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_localizationTriangle (P : ObjectProperty C)
    [P.IsStableUnderRetracts]
    (h : ∀ X : C, ∃ (W Z : C) (a : W ⟶ X) (b : X ⟶ Z) (c : Z ⟶ W⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk a b c ∈ distTriang C ∧ P W ∧ P.rightOrthogonal Z) :
    P.rightOrthogonal.leftOrthogonal ≤ P := by
  intro X hX
  obtain ⟨W, Z, a, b, c, hT, hW, hZ⟩ := h X
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := Triangle.coyoneda_exact₂ _ hT (𝟙 X)
    (by rw [Triangle.mk_mor₂, hX b hZ]; exact comp_zero)
  exact P.prop_of_retract ⟨g, a, hg.symm⟩ hW

/-- **`ᗮ(Pᗮ) ≤ P` from resolutions.** If every object `X` admits a morphism `f : X ⟶ Z` with `Z`
right orthogonal to `P` whose cone lies in `P` — in the intended reading a `K`-injective
resolution, [Stacks, Tag 079P] — then an object left orthogonal to everything right orthogonal
to `P` lies in `P`.

The morphism `f` vanishes, so in the rotated triangle `Z ⟶ W ⟶ X⟦1⟧ ⟶ Z⟦1⟧` the last morphism
is zero and the identity of `X⟦1⟧` factors through `W ⟶ X⟦1⟧`, exhibiting `X⟦1⟧` as a retract
of the cone `W`. -/
lemma leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_resolution (P : ObjectProperty C)
    [P.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] [P.IsStableUnderShift ℤ] [P.IsStableUnderRetracts]
    (h : ∀ X : C, ∃ (Z W : C) (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : Z ⟶ W) (i : W ⟶ X⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g i ∈ distTriang C ∧ P.rightOrthogonal Z ∧ P W) :
    P.rightOrthogonal.leftOrthogonal ≤ P := by
  intro X hX
  obtain ⟨Z, W, f, g, i, hT, hZ, hW⟩ := h X
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := Triangle.coyoneda_exact₃ _ (rot_of_distTriang _ hT) (𝟙 (X⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧))
    (by rw [Triangle.rotate_mor₃, Triangle.mk_mor₁, hX f hZ, Functor.map_zero, neg_zero]
        exact comp_zero)
  have hX1 : P (X⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧) := P.prop_of_retract ⟨s, i, hs.symm⟩ hW
  rwa [P.prop_shift_iff_of_isStableUnderShift] at hX1

end CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

namespace DGCategory

universe v u r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R] (C : DGCategory.{v, u} R)

namespace RightModule

attribute [local implicit_reducible] DGCategory.K

variable {ι : Type*} (G : ι → C.Obj)

section

variable [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated]

/-! ### The acyclics are contained in `Z` -/

omit [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated] in
/-- Each `G i` lies in `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`: its representable is one of the generators of `N`. -/
theorem yonedaInverseImage_obj (i : ι) : yonedaInverseImage C G (G i : C.K) :=
  le_localizingClosure _ _ (ofObj_apply _ i)

omit [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated] in
/-- **The inclusion `Ac ≤ Z`.** A property of objects of `K(C)` whose objects are, up to
isomorphism in `K(C)`, among the `G i` is contained in `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`.

In the intended reading `Ac` is the class of acyclic complexes and `G` enumerates it, which is
the hypothesis the first two steps of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] already carry; the inclusion is then
formal, because `h_{G i}` is a generator of `N`. No acyclicity of the module `h_X` is involved,
and indeed none holds. -/
theorem le_yonedaInverseImage (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K)
    (hG : ∀ X : C.K, Ac X → ∃ i, Nonempty (X ≅ (G i : C.K))) :
    Ac ≤ yonedaInverseImage C G := by
  intro X hX
  obtain ⟨i, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hG X hX
  exact (yonedaLocalizing C G).prop_of_iso (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).mapIso e).symm
    (yonedaInverseImage_obj C G i)

omit [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated] in
/-- **The inclusion `Ac ≤ Z` for the tautological enumeration.** Every property of objects of
`K(C)` is contained in the preimage of the localizing subcategory generated by the
representables of *its own* objects. -/
theorem le_yonedaInverseImage_subtypeVal (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K) :
    Ac ≤ yonedaInverseImage C (fun X : Subtype Ac ↦ (show C.Obj from X.1)) :=
  le_yonedaInverseImage C _ Ac fun X hX ↦ ⟨⟨X, hX⟩, ⟨Iso.refl _⟩⟩

/-! ### `Z` is contained in the acyclics -/

/-- **A representable attached to an object the generators do not see is local for `N`.** Let `D`
be a shift-stable property of objects of `K(C)` such that every morphism from a `G i` to an
object of `D` vanishes. Then `h_Y` lies in `N^⊥` for every `Y` in `D`.

This is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.rightOrthogonal_localizingClosure_iff'`: being local may
be tested on the generators in each degree, and there full faithfulness of `Φ` turns a morphism
`h_{G i} ⟶ (h_Y)⟦n⟧` into a morphism `G i ⟶ Y⟦n⟧`, which vanishes. -/
theorem rightOrthogonal_yonedaLocalizing_obj (D : ObjectProperty C.K) [D.IsStableUnderShift ℤ]
    (hGD : ∀ i, D.leftOrthogonal (G i : C.K)) {Y : C.K} (hY : D Y) :
    (yonedaLocalizing C G).rightOrthogonal (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).obj Y) := by
  have key : ((ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}).rightOrthogonal
      (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).obj Y) := by
    rw [rightOrthogonal_localizingClosure_iff']
    rintro M ⟨i⟩ n g
    obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ :=
      ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).map_surjective
        (g ≫ (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).commShiftIso n).inv.app Y)
    have h0 : ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).map h = 0 := by
      rw [hGD i h (D.le_shift n Y hY)]
      exact Functor.map_zero _ _ _
    exact zero_of_comp_mono _ (hh.symm.trans h0)
  exact key

/-- **Orthogonality descends from the generators to `Z`.** Let `D` be a shift-stable property of
objects of `K(C)` such that every morphism from a `G i` to an object of `D` vanishes. Then every
morphism from an object of `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` to an object of `D` vanishes.

This is the substitute, in this development, for the Neeman–Thomason description of the compact
objects of `N`: by `DGCategory.RightModule.rightOrthogonal_yonedaLocalizing_obj` the
representable `h_Y` is local for `N`, so a morphism into it from `h_X` with `h_X` in `N`
vanishes, and faithfulness of `Φ` carries that back to `K(C)`. -/
theorem yonedaInverseImage_le_leftOrthogonal (D : ObjectProperty C.K) [D.IsStableUnderShift ℤ]
    (hGD : ∀ i, D.leftOrthogonal (G i : C.K)) :
    yonedaInverseImage C G ≤ D.leftOrthogonal := by
  intro X hX Y f hY
  refine ((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).map_injective ?_
  rw [Functor.map_zero]
  exact rightOrthogonal_yonedaLocalizing_obj C G D hGD hY (((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).map f) hX

/-- **The inclusion `Z ≤ Ac`.** Let `Ac` be a property of objects of `K(C)` closed under
isomorphisms, shifts and retracts, let every `G i` lie in `Ac`, and let every object of `K(C)`
admit an `Ac`-resolution — a morphism to an object right orthogonal to `Ac` whose cone lies in
`Ac`, in the intended reading a `K`-injective resolution, [Stacks, Tag 079P]. Then `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`
is contained in `Ac`.

The two halves are `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_le_leftOrthogonal` applied to
`D = Ac.rightOrthogonal`, for which the hypothesis on the generators is precisely that they lie
in `Ac`, and
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_resolution`. The
Neeman–Thomason theorem is not used. -/
theorem yonedaInverseImage_le (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K) [Ac.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms]
    [Ac.IsStableUnderShift ℤ] [Ac.IsStableUnderRetracts]
    (hGAc : ∀ i, Ac (G i : C.K))
    (hres : ∀ X : C.K, ∃ (Z W : C.K) (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : Z ⟶ W) (i : W ⟶ X⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g i ∈ distTriang C.K ∧ Ac.rightOrthogonal Z ∧ Ac W) :
    yonedaInverseImage C G ≤ Ac :=
  (yonedaInverseImage_le_leftOrthogonal C G Ac.rightOrthogonal
      fun i _ f hZ ↦ hZ f (hGAc i)).trans
    (leftOrthogonal_rightOrthogonal_le_of_exists_resolution Ac hres)

/-- **`Z = Ac`.** The subcategory `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` at which
`DGCategory.RightModule.isLocalization_yonedaLift_comp` localizes is exactly `Ac`, as soon as
`G` enumerates `Ac` up to isomorphism in `K(C)` and every object of `K(C)` admits an
`Ac`-resolution. In the intended reading — `C` the differential graded category of complexes of
an abelian category, `Ac` the acyclic complexes, `G` an enumeration of them and the resolutions
the `K`-injective ones — this identifies the target of that localization with the derived
category of the abelian category. -/
theorem yonedaInverseImage_eq (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K) [Ac.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms]
    [Ac.IsStableUnderShift ℤ] [Ac.IsStableUnderRetracts]
    (hG : ∀ X : C.K, Ac X → ∃ i, Nonempty (X ≅ (G i : C.K)))
    (hGAc : ∀ i, Ac (G i : C.K))
    (hres : ∀ X : C.K, ∃ (Z W : C.K) (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : Z ⟶ W) (i : W ⟶ X⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f g i ∈ distTriang C.K ∧ Ac.rightOrthogonal Z ∧ Ac W) :
    yonedaInverseImage C G = Ac :=
  le_antisymm (yonedaInverseImage_le C G Ac hGAc hres) (le_yonedaInverseImage C G Ac hG)

end

end RightModule

end DGCategory

end
